From 21bf460d291012ec1a23266cdb3ad90ba142cb4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:22:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0918/3799] soh: rename D_80153D7C -> sUnusedMessageValue2

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: second UNK_TYPE initialised to 0 further down z_message_PAL.c, likewise with no reader anywhere in the tree.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c b/soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c
index f7cc4731f..4f2c5f362 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_message_PAL.c
@@ -4721,7 +4721,8 @@ void Message_SetTables(void) {
 }
 
 // Appears to be file padding
-UNK_TYPE D_80153D7C = 0x00000000;
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was D_80153D7C: second UNK_TYPE initialised to 0 further down z_message_PAL.c, likewise with no reader anywhere in the tree.
+UNK_TYPE sUnusedMessageValue2 = 0x00000000;  // was D_80153D7C [LLM:GUESS]
 
 // This should be part of z_game_over.c, but cannot be moved there as the entire
 // late_rodata section of this file is in the way
